CERN Open Hardware Licence Version 2 - Permissive

Preamble

CERN has developed this licence to promote collaboration among hardware designers and to provide a legal tool which supports the freedom to use, study, modify, share and distribute hardware designs and products based on those designs. Version 2 of the CERN Open Hardware Licence comes in three variants: CERN-OHL-P (permissive); and two reciprocal variants: CERN-OHL-W (weakly reciprocal) and CERN-OHL-S (strongly reciprocal).

The CERN-OHL-P is a permissive licence. It allows anyone to use, copy, modify, and distribute the licensed material, and to manufacture, use, and sell products based on the licensed material, without any obligation to share the design or to release it under the same licence.

1 Definitions
1.1 “Licence” means this CERN-OHL-P.
1.2 “Source” means information such as design materials or digital code which can be applied to Make or test a Product or to prepare a Product for use, Conveyed as provided in the Licence, and which is not a Product.
1.3 “Covered Source” means Source that is explicitly made available under this Licence.
1.4 “Product” means any device, component, work or physical object, whether in finished or intermediate form, arising from the use, application or processing of Covered Source.
1.5 “Make” means to create or configure something, whether by manufacture, assembly, compiling, loading or applying Covered Source or another Product or otherwise.
1.6 “Available” means that the relevant material is provided, or a visible, reasonable and effective offer to provide it is made, to any person who receives a Product from you.
1.7 “Convey” means to communicate to the public or distribute.
1.8 “Licensor” means any natural or legal person who Conveys Covered Source under this Licence.
1.9 “You” means any natural or legal person exercising rights under this Licence.

2 Applicability
2.1 This Licence governs the use, copying, modification, Conveying of Covered Source and Products, and the Making of Products. By exercising any right granted under this Licence, You irrevocably accept these terms and conditions.
2.2 This Licence is granted by the Licensor directly to You, and shall apply worldwide and without limitation in time.
2.3 You shall not attempt to restrict by contract or otherwise the rights granted under this Licence to other Licensees.
2.4 This Licence is not intended to restrict fair use, fair dealing, or any other similar right.

3 Copying, modifying and Conveying Covered Source
3.1 You may copy and Convey verbatim copies of Covered Source, in any medium, provided You retain all copyright, trademark and patent notices, and an intact copy of this Licence. You may add Your own copyright, trademark and patent notices.
3.2 You may modify Covered Source, other than this Licence. You may copy and Convey such modified Covered Source as if it were verbatim Covered Source, provided You make available the modified Covered Source under a licence of Your choice, and You state clearly that You modified the Covered Source and the date of modification.

4 Making and Conveying Products
4.1 You may Make Products, and/or Convey them, provided You ensure that the recipient is provided with a copy of the Licence and the Covered Source, or a visible, reasonable and effective offer to provide them.

5 Research and Development
5.1 You may Convey Covered Source, modified Covered Source, or Products to a legal entity in which You have a controlling interest, or to a contractor, for the sole purpose of research, development, or testing, provided that they are bound by a non-disclosure agreement to protect the confidentiality of the Covered Source, modified Covered Source or Products, and that they do not Convey them to any third party.

